<description>
Mirror the colored object across the full separator line while swapping its two colors in the original location.

Input structure
- A background grid contains exactly one full foreground row or column separator.
- All other foreground pixels form a source mask entirely on one side of the separator.
- The source mask uses exactly two colors, and its mirror positions on the other side are background.

Rule
- Copy each source pixel to its reflection across the full separator line, preserving its original color.
- Recolor the source pixel in place by swapping the two source colors.
- Leave the separator and all background cells otherwise unchanged.

Key insight
- The separator is an axis of reflection, and the asymmetric two-color source mask is both copied across the axis and color-inverted at its starting side.
</description>
<annotation>
{
  "summary": "Reflect the two-color object across the full separator line and swap its colors at the original side.",
  "type": "symmetry/pattern",
  "src": "two-color foreground mask on one side of the single full separator row or column",
  "dst": "mirror positions on the opposite side of the separator",
  "transform": "copy the source mask to its reflected positions with original colors; recolor the original source pixels by swapping the two source colors; keep the separator unchanged"
}
</annotation>
<generation_spec>
```yaml
spec:
  grid: 9-16 rows x 9-16 cols
  background: 0 (black)
  separator:
    type: single full row or column spanning entire grid width/height
    color: 1 (blue) [observed]
    position: not at edge; both sides have >= 4 cells of depth
  source_sprite:
    location: entirely on one side of separator, at least 1 cell gap from separator
    colors: exactly 2 non-bg non-sep colors (any from palette 2-9)
    pixel_count: 7-11
    bbox: 3-5 rows x 3-5 cols
    connectivity: 1-2 connected components (4-connected)
    density: sparse (contains holes/gaps within bbox)
    mirror_fit: max distance from separator <= opposite side depth (reflection stays in bounds)
    opposite_side: all mirror positions are background (empty)
  total_distinct_colors: exactly 4 (bg + sep + 2 source colors)
  output_rule: |
    1. Copy each source pixel to its reflection across the separator, preserving color.
    2. Swap the two source colors at the original positions.
    3. Separator and background unchanged.

generation_strategy:
  approach: output-first, then strip reflection to get input
  steps:
    1. Choose grid dimensions H x W in 9-16.
    2. Choose separator orientation (h or v) and position ensuring both sides >= 4 deep.
    3. Pick 2 source colors from palette 2-9, plus sep_color=1.
    4. Design a sprite with 2 colors, 7-11 pixels, bbox 3-5 x 3-5, with holes.
    5. Place sprite on one side with >= 1 cell gap to separator and reflection fits on other side.
    6. Build output by reflecting sprite across separator and swapping colors at original side.
    7. Strip the reflected copy to produce the input (keep only original-side sprite + separator).
```
